  "improvements": [
    "Refreshed the complete palace perimeter, preserving the cour d’honneur recess.",
    "Source polygon collision retains the actual open forecourt.",
    "Applied the complete source-part profile pass: Complete 263 mapped building-part solids at their explicit height/min_height, unioned in vertical intervals. Only the source primary residual uses its12m height; broad18m and15.7m parts,4m plinth,14m columns and elevated trim retain their actual source boundaries.",
    "Walls are warm cream limestone (#e1d6bc) over a darker rusticated ground floor instead of the mapped colour name palegoldenrod, which read olive in shade; each wall panel has one window on the three storeys the palace shows: arched ground floor, tall first floor, lower second floor."
  ],
  "remainingGaps": [
    "Mapped hip roof rises remain represented by their exact outer height envelopes; decorative curvature is simplified.",
    "Main entry door/marquee and rail details remain independent-photo estimates.",
    "Neighbour overlap, terrain support and tourist-scene context need the separate district/scene pass; isolated model pictures do not establish complete parity.",
    "Storey heights, window sizes and the colour come from the walk scene and Street View from Piata Revolutiei (2024, viewed as reference only; not stored or published); estimates."
  ],
